# Phase 15 R1: check every text file out with LF, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Every blob in the repository is already LF. Without this file, a checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true (Git for Windows sets it system-wide) rewrites the working
# tree as CRLF. That breaks more than `prettier --check`: hello-remote's
# index.html pins its inline <script> with a sha256 CSP source computed over the
# LF bytes, and a CRLF copy of the same script hashes differently, so the
# browser would silently refuse to run it. See docs/plans/phase-15.md.
* text=auto eol=lf
